---
import FunctionCatalog from "./FunctionCatalog.vue";
---

<section class="section catalog-section" id="functions">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head reveal">
      <div class="eyebrow">Function catalog</div>
      <h2>What can you intercept? About eighty common calls.</h2>
      <p>
        retrace ships with prototypes for nearly three hundred libc functions out of the box. Below
        is a curated tour of the most-traced, grouped by what they're for. Click any function to see
        its signature and the one-liner to trace it. Use <code class="mono">retrace list-functions</code>
        for the full list.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="reveal">
      <FunctionCatalog client:visible />
    </div>

    <p class="more-link reveal">
      Looking for <code>socket</code>, <code>connect</code>, <code>send</code>, <code>recv</code>?
      Network functions are not yet in the default intercept set — tracked in
      <a href="https://github.com/riboseinc/retrace/issues">issues</a>. Until they ship, use
      <code>strace</code> for raw syscall-level network observation, or write a custom action.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
.catalog-section {
  background:
    radial-gradient(ellipse 60% 40% at 50% 0%, rgba(242, 180, 65, 0.03), transparent 60%);
}

.more-link {
  margin-top: 28px;
  text-align: center;
  font-size: 13px;
  color: var(--color-dim);
  line-height: 1.6;
}
.more-link code {
  font-family: var(--font-mono);
  font-size: 12px;
  color: var(--color-text);
  background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05);
  padding: 1px 5px;
  border-radius: 3px;
}
.more-link a {
  color: var(--color-see);
  border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(94, 227, 255, 0.3);
}
</style>
